---
import RecipeLayout from "../../components/layout/RecipeLayout.astro";
import { recipes } from "../../data/relatedContent";
import makkaroni from "../../assets/images/genuss/makkaroni.png";

const ingredients = [
  "2 onions",
  "2 garlic cloves",
  "400 g waxy potatoes",
  "150 g diced bacon",
  "500 ml vegetable broth",
  "250 ml cream",
  "250 g macaroni",
  "60 g strong, aged Bergkäse (Alpine mountain cheese), grated",
  "Salt & black pepper to taste",
];
const steps = [
  "Peel the onions, garlic, and potatoes. Slice the onions into rings, thinly slice the garlic, and dice the potatoes.",
  "Cook the bacon, onions, and garlic in a skillet until the onions are golden and the bacon is lightly crisp. Transfer to a plate and set aside.",
  "Bring the vegetable broth and cream to a boil in a saucepan. Add the potatoes and macaroni, cover, and simmer over low heat for about 10 minutes, until the macaroni is al dente.",
  "Stir in the grated Bergkäse until melted and creamy. Season with salt and black pepper to taste. Divide among plates and top with the bacon and onion mixture.",
];
---

<RecipeLayout
  lang="en"
  pageTitle="Älpler Makkaroni – Domaće"
  description="Alpine macaroni with potatoes, Bergkäse and cream, topped with golden onions and bacon. A comforting dinner for four, ready in about 35 minutes."
  category="Cooking"
  title="Älpler Makkaroni"
  image={makkaroni}
  imageAlt="Two plates of creamy macaroni and potatoes topped with golden onions and bacon, with apple sauce on the side"
  summary="Think of it as Alpine mac and cheese: macaroni and potatoes in a creamy Bergkäse sauce, topped with golden onions and bacon."
  totalTime="PT35M"
  meta={[{ icon: "clock", label: "Total time", value: "35 minutes" }, { icon: "users", label: "Makes", value: "4 servings" }]}
  ingredients={ingredients}
  steps={steps}
  stepIngredients={[[0, 1, 2], [3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8]]}
  ingredientNote="I use a strong, aged Bergkäse, an Alpine mountain cheese with plenty of flavor. If you can’t find it, Gruyère is a good substitute."
  tipTitle="Make it your own"
  tipText="The onions are worth taking your time with. Let them cook until deeply golden for plenty of flavor and a little crispness around the edges."
  safetyTipTitle="Keep an eye on the pot"
  safetyTipText="The pasta and potatoes cook together, so give them an occasional stir and add a splash of stock if the sauce gets too thick."
  relatedItems={[recipes.boeufStroganoff, recipes.focaccia]}
>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <p>There’s a reason Älpler Makkaroni is traditionally served with apple sauce. A spoonful alongside the savory pasta might seem unexpected, but it cuts through the richness beautifully.</p>
    <p>It’s an uncomplicated dish, made from the kind of ingredients that keep well in a pantry and come together in one pot. I like mine with plenty of browned onions on top and the apple sauce right there on the plate.</p>
  </Fragment>
  <h2>Macaroni and potatoes, cooked together</h2>
  <p>The macaroni and potatoes cook in the broth and cream before the cheese is stirred in. Prepare the onion and bacon topping in a separate frying pan, then add it just before serving.</p>
</RecipeLayout>
